The three SMARD endpoints have only placeholder .yaml files, so the CLI dumps their answer as raw YAML. The shapes are measured (2026-10-20): smard_indices answers with a list of timestamps, smard_timeseries with positional pairs [timestamp, value], smard_table with the rows under series[0].values[] - one level deeper than the OpenAPI spec describes. Two extensions of the formatter come with it: keyed_matrix takes the column list from the template when the header is missing, and a table cell that holds a nested value shows it as JSON instead of staying silently empty. Test: t/smard_templates.t checks the 21 files, renders the three measured answers and covers both extensions.

